<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sullivan Expedition</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1779">1779</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Sullivan-Clinton Expedition, Sullivan Campaign, Sullivan-Clinton Campaign</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sullivan Expedition was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> military campaign of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-revolutionary-war">American Revolutionary War</a>, from June to October 1779, against the four British-allied nations of the Haudenosaunee (Iroquois) Confederacy in what is now <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a>. Ordered by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-washington">George Washington</a> after Haudenosaunee and Loyalist raids on the Wyoming Valley and Cherry Valley, four Continental Army <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brigade">brigades</a> under John Sullivan and James Clinton carried out a scorched-earth campaign, razing 40 villages with their crops and food stores. Just over 5,000 Haudenosaunee fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fort-niagara">Fort Niagara</a>, where many starved or froze to death that winter. Some scholars describe the campaign as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genocide">genocide</a>, a term that is disputed.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sullivan-expedition.jpg" alt="Sullivan Expedition" width="330" height="186" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sullivan01.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In 1779 the <b>Sullivan Expedition</b> destroyed some forty Haudenosaunee towns and their crops, and the Treaty of Paris of 1783 made no provision for Britain’s Native allies.</blockquote><a href="/empire/iroquois-confederacy">Iroquois Confederacy · Into the Present</a></li><li><blockquote>The Revolution broke the League apart, and after the <b>Sullivan Expedition</b> of 1779 destroyed 40 to 60 towns, more than 5,000 Haudenosaunee fled to British Canada.</blockquote><a href="/societies/haudenosaunee">Social Hierarchy of the Haudenosaunee</a></li></ul></section>
